A||||3||artherd||Rebuild?||||3||
Z||000000||artherd||09-17-2001||04:47 AM||||One hundred years from now, I hope Mankind will look back to the day when a World united in an unprecedented and universal way against hate and injustice, a World rocked not into chaos, but into global brother and sisterhood and love for each other near and far.<P>A day the World changed forever, a World turned on it's ear as seperate countries, a World that rose from the ground united as One. <P>A World that *rebuilt* the World Trade Center towers, Taller and Brighter and more Gleaming than ever before, a giant pair of middle fingers in the face of evil, sending a crystal clear message that you CANNOT enslave truely free spirits, that Freedom, nay, Humanity, Prevailed That Day!!<P><BR>Best!<BR>Ben.<P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000001||Formula||09-17-2001||09:14 AM||||I think they should make 1 220 story tower, that would be tall.||||reg||1
Z||000002||SteveJ||09-17-2001||09:55 AM||||With today's communications there is no need for those old towers in the sky. Once they were needed to keep people close for communication but today it just isn't needed. They always were an engineering tour d'force but what is needed is low tech. Look how much better the Pentagon made out.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fformula88||09-17-2001||10:38 AM||||I would also like to see the towers rebuilt... but am not so sure they will be.  It has nothing to do with security, and everything to do with modern day urban planning.  There has been a major move away from the collossal sky scrapers for many reasons.  Not only the communications factors mentioned, but also environmental impacts.  <P>On the other hand, I do like the single 220 story building idea!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Instead of two middle fingers, we'll give them one really big one!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero2m6siga.JPG">     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/halfpole.gif"> <P>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||1
